---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// Plain legal page -- no PageHero/i18n-JSON here on purpose (this is a
// legal document, not marketing copy that should be auto-translated).
// Written to satisfy Google's OAuth app verification requirement (a real,
// publicly reachable privacy policy that specifically discloses what
// Google user data this app accesses and how -- see the "Google Calendar
// data" section below, which is the section Google's reviewers actually
// check). Entity: Mielikkix AS, a Norwegian company currently mid-
// registration (bank account + Brønnøysund registration in process as of
// 2026-08-28) -- worded below as "in process," not as an already-completed
// registration, since claiming a finished registration before it exists
// would misstate our own legal status. Revisit this wording once
// registration completes. No registered postal address is published yet
// for the same reason -- email contact is sufficient for a privacy policy
// and doesn't require one.
const lastUpdated = "August 28, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Mielikkix collects, uses, and protects data -- including what Google Calendar data this app accesses and why."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose-legal mt-10 space-y-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
      <section>
        <p>
          Mielikkix ("Mielikkix," "we," "us") provides an AI-powered chat, booking, and voice
          receptionist platform that businesses embed on their own websites and phone lines. This
          policy explains what data we collect, how we use it, and -- specifically, since this app
          integrates with Google Calendar -- exactly what Google user data we access and why.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Mielikkix is operated by <strong>Mielikkix AS</strong>, a company being registered in
          Norway (registration in process). Mielikkix AS is the data controller for the personal
          data described in this policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Who this policy covers</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong>Businesses</strong> that create a Mielikkix account (the dashboard user) to
            configure and run their chatbot, booking assistant, or voice receptionist.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>End visitors</strong> who interact with a business's Mielikkix-powered chat
            widget, booking flow, or phone line -- these are the business's own customers, not
            Mielikkix's.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Data we collect</h2>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">From businesses (dashboard accounts)</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Name, email, and hashed password used to sign in.</li>
          <li>Business profile details you provide (business name, industry, uploaded FAQs, documents, and products used to ground your chatbot's answers).</li>
          <li>Plan and billing tier selection (no payment card details are processed or stored by Mielikkix directly today).</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">From end visitors, via a business's widget/phone line</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Chat messages sent to a business's chatbot, and the AI's replies, kept as a conversation history for that business (retention length depends on the business's plan).</li>
          <li>Lead details a visitor submits (name, email, phone, message), shared with that business.</li>
          <li>Booking details (name, email, phone, requested appointment time) when a visitor books an appointment through Booking Assistant.</li>
          <li>For phone calls to a business's Voice Receptionist line: the call audio is transcribed to text by our telephony provider to carry on the conversation; call transcripts are held only in memory for the duration of the call today and are not currently written to a database.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="google-calendar-data">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Google Calendar data (Google API Services)</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Booking Assistant lets a business connect their own Google Calendar so the assistant can
          check real availability and create real appointments on that business's behalf. This is
          entirely opt-in: a business only connects if they choose to use Booking Assistant, by
          signing in with their own Google account through Google's own consent screen.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">When a business connects their calendar, we request exactly two Google Calendar scopes:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">calendar.freebusy</code> -- read-only
            access to when the connected calendar is busy or free. We never read the contents,
            titles, descriptions, or attendees of a business's existing calendar events -- only
            whether a given time slot is already taken.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">calendar.events</code> -- lets
            Mielikkix create new calendar events representing appointments booked through the
            assistant, with the visitor who booked as an attendee (so Google emails them a
            calendar invite directly). We do not read, modify, or delete events we did not
            create.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We also request basic account email (<code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">userinfo.email</code>)
          solely so the business's own dashboard can show them which Google account is connected
          (e.g. "Connected as: owner@theirbusiness.com").
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong>How this data is stored:</strong> the OAuth refresh token Google issues is
          encrypted at rest before it is ever written to our database, using a symmetric key held
          only on our own servers. It is decrypted only in memory, immediately before making a
          calendar API call on that business's behalf, and is never logged, emailed, or exposed to
          any other business.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong>How this data is used:</strong> solely to check real-time availability and create
          the specific appointments a business's own visitors book through that business's
          Booking Assistant. We do not use Google user data for advertising, do not sell it, do not
          share it with any third party except the Google Calendar API itself (to perform the
          calendar action) and the business that owns the connection, and do not use it to train
          any AI model.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          A business can disconnect their calendar at any time from their own Settings page, which
          deletes the stored refresh token immediately. Disconnecting does not delete
          already-created calendar events (those are removed the normal way, directly in Google
          Calendar).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Mielikkix's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
          <a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            class="text-indigo-600 underline"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a
          >, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Other service providers we use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We rely on the following third-party services to operate Mielikkix. Each only receives
          the data needed to perform its specific function:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li><strong>Groq</strong> -- processes chat/voice messages to generate AI replies.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Calendar API</strong> -- as described above, for Booking Assistant.</li>
          <li><strong>Twilio</strong> -- carries and transcribes phone calls to a business's Voice Receptionist number.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> -- delivers transactional emails (lead notifications, booking notifications, password resets).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Data retention</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Conversation history is retained according to a business's plan (from 7 days up to
          unlimited, depending on tier). A business can delete their uploaded documents, FAQs, and
          products at any time from their dashboard. Account deletion is currently handled by
          contacting us directly (see "Contact us" below) rather than a self-serve control; we
          delete the requesting business's account data once we've verified the request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Security</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Passwords are hashed, never stored in plain text. OAuth refresh tokens (including Google
          Calendar tokens) are encrypted at rest. Dashboard sessions use httpOnly authentication
          cookies. Access to a business's own data is scoped to that business only.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          As Mielikkix AS is a Norwegian company, processing of personal data is governed by the
          Norwegian Personal Data Act and the GDPR as it applies in Norway. Depending on your
          relationship to us, you have the right to:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete personal data.</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your personal data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
          <li>Restrict or object to certain processing.</li>
          <li>Receive your data in a portable format, where technically feasible.</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent at any time, where processing is based on consent.</li>
          <li>
            Lodge a complaint with the Norwegian Data Protection Authority
            (<a href="https://www.datatilsynet.no" class="text-indigo-600 underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Datatilsynet</a>)
            if you believe your data has been processed unlawfully.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We process a business's account data to perform our contract with that business
          (providing the chat/booking/voice platform), and we process an end visitor's data on
          behalf of, and under instruction from, the business they contacted -- Mielikkix acts as
          a data processor for that visitor data, and the business itself is the controller for
          their own customers. To exercise any of the above rights, contact us at the address
          below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update this policy as Mielikkix's features change. Material changes will be
          reflected by updating the "Last updated" date above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Contact us</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Questions about this policy or your data: <a href="mailto:post@mielikkix.no" class="text-indigo-600 underline">post@mielikkix.no</a>.
          Mielikkix AS, Norway (company registration in process; a registered postal address will
          be added here once registration completes).
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
